  "_source_stem": "Hinsdale2022",
  "_notes": "Read from the Town Clerk's handwritten counts on the printed sample ballot (owner-supplied scan 4955_001.pdf p2), 2026-08-27, at up to 1400 dpi. The scan clipped the left margin and the clerk had hand-restored the missing leading characters over the printed text; the Select Board 2-year write-ins survive as the tails \"...llins\" and \"...nica\", read as Collins and Monica -- Bartholomew J. Collins and Monica J. Montferret are the printed Select Board 3-year candidates on the same page and no other name on it fits. Robert Cimini's total is 130: the third digit is a closed round loop identical to the zero in Bonnie Conner's 130 in the same hand, and unlike every 5 on the page. ONE CELL IS NOT READ: a Shaun Galliher write-in on the Finance Committee 3-year line carries a single mark that is either 4 or 11 -- it matches neither the clerk's 4 (descender), 1 (full-height slant) nor 6 (closed loop) -- so the line is recorded here and deliberately NOT carried as a candidate rather than approximated. Galliher is separately recorded taking the 2-year Finance Committee seat with 17. The clerk's marginalia record whether each write-in accepted: Vivian Mason \"Refused NO\" for Assessor 3-year and \"will take\" for Assessor 1-year; Richard Roussin \"accept\" for Planning Board 4-year; \"NO\" against Keith Harrison on Planning Board 2-year; Shaun Galliher \"takes 2 yr\". These are dispositions, not vote counts. NO BALLOTS-CAST FIGURE IS PRINTED on this page -- the only one of the five in the scan without one. The floor is 174, because Select Board 3-year is vote-for-one and Collins 89 + Montferret 85 = 174 before any blank. So ballots x seats cannot be closed and no turnout is asserted.",
  "document": {
    "heading_verbatim": "Annual Town Election, Hinsdale, Massachusetts, May 14, 2022 -- List of Candidates for Town Office",
    "turnout_verbatim": "not printed; floor of 174 ballots from the vote-for-one Select Board 3-year race (89 + 85)"
